course: dictionary
lesson: 9594
title: Stress: worry, emphasis and sound
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Stress has more than one meaning, so context tells you which one you need. Read the words around it. «Many places no longer give goldfish as fair prizes, because a fish in a small bag is stressed and often dies soon after.» Here stressed means under pressure and harmed, not worried in your mind.
explain: «Listen for words the speaker stresses, because they show what matters.» Here stress means to say something is very important, so the speaker says it more strongly. Ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
explain: Stress also changes how a word sounds. In «be-GIN», the beat falls on the second part, so you say that part louder. Say «REcord» and «reCORD» out loud and you will hear the stress move. Stress can be a force too, like the pressure on a bridge.
fact: Stress can mean a feeling of worry and pressure when you have too much to do.
fact: To stress something means to say it is very important.
fact: Stress in a word means saying one part louder or stronger, like «TA-ble».
fact: Stress can also be a force that pushes, pulls or presses on something, such as a beam in a bridge.
fact: A little stress before a test is normal, and breathing, exercise, sleep and talking help.
exercise: «Ben feels stress before his spelling test.» What does stress mean here? | A type of sweet | A loud, sharp noise | A kind of spelling | *A feeling of worry and pressure
exercise: «Listen for words the speaker stresses, because they show what matters.» What does stresses mean here? | Writes them in a list | Forgets them quickly | *Says them as very important | Says them quietly
exercise: In the word «be-GIN», which part gets the stress? | The first part, be | Both parts are said equally | *The second part, gin | Neither part is said aloud
test: «REcord» and «reCORD» are spelled the same. What changes when the stress moves? | Nothing at all changes | Only its length changes | Its spelling changes | *How the word sounds, and sometimes its meaning
test: «The engineers checked the stress on each steel beam.» What is stress here? | A type of paint | A feeling of worry | *The force that pushes, pulls or presses on the beam | A loud warning
exam: Priya says «The teacher stressed that the test was important.» What does stressed mean? | Said it was not important at all | Lost the test paper | *Said it was very important | Drew a picture of the test
